#import "../lib.typ": *

#section(
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(169)

    This affords a good drill and a good test of accuracy in applying
    movement. The last downward stroke in capital H is a left curve, is it
    not? Study the direction of the pen in making it, and then strike boldly.
    This will be a good drill to practice frequently at the beginning of a
    lesson.
  ], lines: 6, examples: ("drill-169-h", "drill-169-h-2")),
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(170)

    Use your eyes, focus your mind upon your work, study and practice
    earnestly, and you will be pleased with the results.
  ], lines: 6, examples: ("drill-170", "drill-170-2")),
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(171)

    Movement drills for a few minutes and then the following:

    Practice the combination of capitals several times before making the small
    letters. Such repeated effort will be helpful.
  ], lines: 6, examples: ("drill-171", "drill-171-2")),
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(172)
  ], lines: 6, examples: ("drill-172", "drill-172-2")),
)
